  "question": {
    "text": "Two coils <math><mi>&#39;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi><mi>&#39;</mi></math> and <math><mi>&#39;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Q</mi><mi>&#39;</mi></math> are separated by some distance. When a current of <math><mn>3</mn><mi>&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math> flows through coil <math><mi>&#39;</mi><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>&#39;</mi></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo></math> a magnetic flux of <math><msup><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup><mi>&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">W</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">b</mi></math> passes through <math><mi>&#39;</mi><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Q</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>&#39;</mi></mrow></msup><mo>.</mo></math> No current is passed through <math><mi>&#39;</mi><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Q</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>&#39;</mi></mrow></msup><mo>.</mo></math> When no current passes through <math><mi>&#39;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi><mi>&#39;</mi></math> and a current of <math><mn>2</mn><mi>&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math> passes through <math><mi>&#39;</mi><msup><mrow><mi>Q</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>&#39;</mi></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo></math> the flux through <math><mi>&#39;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi><mi>&#39;</mi></math> is:",
